example

# generated native folders (ExportOptions.plist is the one keeper: the
# TestFlight upload step needs it and it holds no secrets)
/ios/*
!/ios/ExportOptions.plist
# VerseWidget is hand-authored source (Swift + assets + fonts + verses.json), not
# generated by prebuild. Keep it in git. The .xcodeproj stays ignored but the
# target is reproducible via scripts/add_widget_target.rb.
!/ios/VerseWidget/
# The Podfile is hand-maintained too, and its post_install now carries the fix
# that makes Debug builds link at all (see trial-and-error.md). Losing it to a
# regenerated ios/ would silently bring the failure back. Podfile.lock stays
# ignored: it is derived, and `pod install` rebuilds it.
!/ios/Podfile
/android

# local env files (Supabase keys, Google client IDs, Sentry DSN)
.env
env.hosted.backup

# .env.production was tracked until 2026-08-02, which put the hosted anon key,
# the Google client IDs and the Sentry DSN in a PUBLIC repo. Every value in it
# is EXPO_PUBLIC_ and therefore ships inside the app bundle anyway, so nothing
# secret leaked, but a public repo is no place for it and the DSN invites event
# spam. Untracked now; the file itself must STAY on disk and keep this exact
# name, because Expo loads it automatically for Release bundling (see the
# TestFlight pipeline in CLAUDE.md). A fresh clone will not have it: rebuild it
# from env.hosted.backup before archiving, or Release will bundle an undefined
# Supabase URL.
.env.production

# generated privacy-policy page. The workflow builds it fresh on every publish;
# the source of truth is docs/privacy-policy.md.
_site/

